---
title: Master Services Agreement
parties:
  - Acme Corp, a Delaware corporation ("Provider")
  - Globex Inc, a New York corporation ("Client")
effective_date: 2026-01-15
---

# Definitions

[[define:Agreement|this Master Services Agreement, including all Exhibits and Schedules attached hereto]] means this Master Services Agreement, together with all Exhibits and Schedules attached hereto or incorporated by reference, as may be amended from time to time in accordance with [[ref:sec-amendment]].

[[define:Confidential Information|non-public information disclosed by either party in connection with this Agreement]] means non-public information disclosed by either party in connection with the [[Agreement]], whether marked confidential or not, subject to the exclusions in [[ref:sec-exclusions]].

[[define:Services|the services described in each Statement of Work]] means the services described in one or more Statements of Work executed by both parties under this [[Agreement]].

# Confidential Information {#sec-confidential-info}

## Obligations

Each party agrees to protect the other party's [[Confidential Information]] using at least the same degree of care it uses to protect its own confidential information, and in no event less than reasonable care.[^care-standard]

## Exclusions {#sec-exclusions}

### Publicly available information

[[Confidential Information]] does not include information that was already publicly available at the time of disclosure.

### Independently developed information

[[Confidential Information]] does not include information that the receiving party can demonstrate, by written records, was independently developed without reference to the disclosing party's [[Confidential Information]].

#### Burden of proof

The receiving party bears the burden of establishing the exclusion under this clause by clear and convincing evidence.[^burden]

# Term and Termination

## Term

This [[Agreement]] commences on the Effective Date and continues until terminated as provided in [[ref:sec-termination-convenience]] or [[ref:sec-termination-cause]].

## Termination for convenience {#sec-termination-convenience}

Either party may terminate this [[Agreement]] for convenience upon sixty (60) days' prior written notice to the other party.

## Termination for cause {#sec-termination-cause}

Either party may terminate this [[Agreement]] immediately upon written notice if the other party materially breaches any provision of this [[Agreement]] and fails to cure such breach within thirty (30) days after receiving written notice describing the breach in reasonable detail.

# Amendment {#sec-amendment}

This [[Agreement]] may only be amended by a written instrument signed by authorized representatives of both parties. No oral modification, waiver, or course of dealing shall be effective to amend this [[Agreement]].

# Governing Law

This [[Agreement]] is governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles.

[[signature-block]]

[^care-standard]: This "at least as protective" formulation is the market standard for mutual NDAs and MSAs alike; see generally ABA Model Confidentiality Agreement commentary.

[^burden]: Some jurisdictions apply a "preponderance of the evidence" standard here instead; confirm against the governing-law clause in [[ref:sec-termination-cause]]'s surrounding Article before relying on "clear and convincing" in a non-Delaware agreement.
